<title>THAILAND: Thai bourse suspends six firms.</title>
<headline>Thai bourse suspends six firms.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Stock Exchange of Thailand said it suspended six listed firms from trading for one day on Thursday and later from February 3 after the companies failed to submit annual business plans to the bourse by December 31.</p>
<p>The bourse said in a statement their suspension from February 3 would be lifted once the companies complied with the bourse's regulations on revealing business operating plans.</p>
<p>The bourse said in a statement that the suspended firms were Phuket Island Plc, Semiconductor Ventures International Plc, Surat Canning Plc, Siam Agro-Industry Pineapple and Others Plc, Earth Industrial Plc, and Unicord Plc.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662)-2529950-3</p>
